KEYBOARD - Computah OS library
(generated from docs/API.md)

Key codes and modifier state. Key codes in
key_down/key_up signals are GLFW key codes (not
the LWJGL 2 codes OpenComputers uses); use
keyboard.keys instead of numbers.

keyboard.keys

Table mapping names to codes and codes back to
names: letters a–z, digits "0"–"9", enter, back
(backspace), tab, space, escape, delete, insert,
up, down, left, right, home, end, pageUp,
pageDown, f1–f12, lshift, rshift, lcontrol,
rcontrol, lmenu, rmenu (alt), numpad0–numpad9,
numpadenter and punctuation names (minus, equals,
comma, period, slash, semicolon, apostrophe,
lbracket, rbracket, backslash, grave).

  local _, _, char, code = event.pull("key_down")
  if code == keyboard.keys.up then ... end

keyboard.isKeyDown(code) -> boolean

Whether a key (code or name) is held, according to
the key_down/key_up signals seen so far.

keyboard.isControlDown() -> boolean

Whether either Control key is held.

keyboard.isShiftDown() -> boolean

Whether either Shift key is held.

keyboard.isAltDown() -> boolean

Whether either Alt key is held.

keyboard.isControl(char) -> boolean

Whether a character code is a control character
(below 32, or 127–159).
